  217                   / Write a block of ascii text out.
  218                   / Write out a string produced by ascii until a word containing
  219                   / only 0 is seen, the starting address is in the ac,
  220                   / ascii <whatever>
  221                   /
  222                   / Include this before using it or declaring text that uses
  223                   / the character defines, below.
  224                   /
  225                   / Output goes to SBS channel 0 which must be in ascii mode.
  226                   / On call, AC contains the address of the text block.
  227                   / Insert this at the desired point in code.
  228                   / Call via jda txtasc.

